-- title:
--   Dual of an invertible module as ideal sheaf of Z(s)
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $M$ be a sheaf of modules over the sheaf of rings of $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $M$ along the inclusion $U \to X$ is isomorphic to the unit module $\mathcal O_U$. Let $s \colon \mathbb 1 \to M$ be a morphism from the unit object, i.e. a global section of $M$. Let `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s` be the least ideal sheaf datum $J$ on $X$ with $J(U)$ containing, for every affine open $U$, the ideal `coeffIdeal s U` generated by all coefficients of $s$ relative to trivialisations over $U$; assume it is invertible in the sense that each point of $X$ lies in some basic open $X_f$, $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $U$ affine open, for which the ideal of the datum at the affine basic open attached to $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. Then there is an isomorphism $\psi$ from the dual $\operatorname{\mathcal Hom}(M,\mathbb 1)$ onto the module of the ideal sheaf datum `zeroSchemeIdeal s` — the kernel of the map from $\mathcal O_X$ to the pushforward of the structure sheaf of the associated closed subscheme — such that $\psi$ followed by the canonical inclusion `moduleι` of that module into $\mathcal O_X$ is the evaluation map $\lambda \mapsto \lambda(s)$, i.e. `sectionDual s`.
--
--   This is the identification $\mathcal M^\vee \cong \mathcal I_{Z(s)}$ of the dual of an invertible module with the ideal sheaf of the zero scheme of a section, under the hypothesis that this zero scheme is an effective Cartier divisor; the evaluation map at $s$ is exhibited as the composite of the isomorphism with the inclusion of the ideal sheaf. It feeds the dual statement $\mathcal M \cong \mathcal O_X(Z(s))$ used in the treatment of relative Cartier divisors and the relative Picard functor.
